/* Deep lessons — Greedy algorithms (greedy).
 *
 * The hard part of greedy is not the code. Every greedy algorithm in this
 * track is five lines long; what separates a correct one from a wrong one is
 * an argument, and arguments are exactly what a shallow lesson leaves out.
 *
 * So this track teaches the two proofs FIRST — exchange and stays-ahead — and
 * then treats each classic problem as a place to run one of them. The closing
 * stages go the other way: a stage on why greedy fails, and one on the
 * structure (matroids) that says in advance when it cannot.
 *
 * Original text and diagrams. Nothing copied from any source.
 */

import type { DeepLesson } from "../deep-lesson";

